---
import MailLink from '../components/MailLink.astro';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { CONTACT_URL, LEGAL_UPDATED, OPERATOR } from '../site.config';
import { formatDate } from '../lib/devices';
---

<Base
  title="Privacy and cookies"
  description="Workswithwhat sets no cookies and runs no analytics or trackers. What our hosting providers process to deliver and protect the site, and your rights."
  crumbs={[{ name: 'Privacy and cookies', path: '/privacy/' }]}
>
  <h1>Privacy and cookies</h1>
  <p class="muted">Last updated <time datetime={LEGAL_UPDATED}>{formatDate(LEGAL_UPDATED)}</time></p>

  <p class="callout">
    <strong>Short version:</strong> we don't set cookies, we don't run analytics, ads or tracking scripts, and we
    don't ask you for any personal data. That's why there is no cookie banner.
  </p>

  <h2>Who is responsible</h2>
  <p>
    The data controller is the operator of Workswithwhat{OPERATOR.name && <> ({OPERATOR.name})</>}, as listed in the
    <a href="/legal/">legal notice</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>What gets processed when you visit</h2>
  <p>
    The site is a set of static pages. To deliver them, one provider handles your request and, like any web server,
    sees technical data such as your IP address, browser user agent, the page requested and the time:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Cloudflare</strong> (Cloudflare, Inc.) hosts the files on Cloudflare Pages and serves them quickly over
      HTTPS, blocking attacks. See <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/trust-hub/gdpr/" rel="nofollow noopener">Cloudflare's GDPR page</a>.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We use this only to deliver the site and keep it secure, which is our legitimate interest under Article 6(1)(f)
    GDPR. We don't receive or keep personal access logs, don't build profiles, and don't combine this with other
    data. Cloudflare is based in the United States and certified under the EU-U.S. Data Privacy Framework, which
    covers transfers of data from the EU.
  </p>

  <h2>Cookies</h2>
  <p>
    Workswithwhat sets no cookies and uses no local storage. Cloudflare may set a strictly necessary security cookie
    (such as <code>cf_clearance</code>) if it has to check that a request isn't automated. These cookies only protect
    the site, don't track you, and are exempt from consent under the ePrivacy rules (in Spain, Article 22.2 of the LSSI).
  </p>

  <h2>If you contact us</h2>
  <p>
    You can send corrections and questions {OPERATOR.email && <>by email or </>}through <a href={CONTACT_URL}>GitHub issues</a>. Issues are public and subject to
    GitHub's privacy statement, so don't include personal data you don't want published.
    {OPERATOR.email && <> If you email us at <MailLink />, the message is forwarded by Cloudflare Email Routing to a Gmail inbox (Google). We use it only to answer you and delete it when it's no longer needed.</>}
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    You can ask for access to, correction or deletion of your personal data, or object to its processing, by
    contacting us as described in the legal notice. You can also complain to your data protection authority; in Spain
    that is the <a href="https://www.aepd.es/" rel="nofollow noopener">Agencia Española de Protección de Datos (AEPD)</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    If we ever add analytics or anything else that processes personal data or sets non-essential cookies, we will
    update this page first and ask for consent where the law requires it.
  </p>
</Base>
